        "description": "Take one authorised file away with you (BUG-28).\n\nA generated document was previewable and nothing else: the only way to get a\nreport Raiker wrote onto disk was to select the preview text and paste it\nsomewhere. This is the byte download, and it is deliberately narrow:\n\n* **Authorisation is the stored reference**, exactly as for preview — this\n  session, this attachment, this owner — so a download can never reach a file\n  the same person could not already open. 404 for anything else; a 403 would\n  confirm the id exists.\n* **Nothing is served as something the browser will run.** The response is\n  always ``application/octet-stream`` with an attachment disposition and\n  ``nosniff``. HTML, SVG and script-bearing formats are not upload types\n  here, and even so the browser is never invited to interpret a download.\n* **The filename is rebuilt, not echoed.** ``_download_filename`` strips\n  anything that could break out of the header or name a path.\n* **The download is evidence.** Every one appends ``attachment_downloaded``\n  with metadata only — id, name, type, size — never the bytes.",
        "operationId": "download_attachment_api_sessions__session_id__attachments__attachment_id__download_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "session_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Session Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "attachment_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Attachment Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Download Attachment"
      }
    },
